<title>ISRAEL: Israel to offer small high-tech firms tax breaks.</title>
<headline>Israel to offer small high-tech firms tax breaks.</headline>
<dateline>TEL AVIV 1996-11-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Israel's Industry and Trade Ministry said on Wednesday that it was extending tax benefits on research and development costs to smaller high technology companies with revenues of less than $1 million.</p>
<p>The new rules, which were drawn up by a committee headed by chief scientist Yehoshua Gleitman, must be signed by Finance Minister Dan Meridor before they can take force.</p>
<p>Until now, tax benefits were only available for high-tech companies with revenues of more than $1 million.</p>
<p>- Tel Aviv newsroom, 972-3-537-2211</p>
